  "rules": [
    "Apply aggressive downward bias correction immediately following any negative sentiment spike (-0.33 or lower), as the model consistently fails to anticipate the subsequent 10-15% price collapse.",
    "Reduce forecast horizon by 15-20% for the first 10 days after a sentiment shift; the model exhibits a severe lag, predicting a slow drift while actual prices crash rapidly.",
    "Override model mean-reversion logic during downtrends: do not allow forecasts to stabilize or rise until the true price has demonstrated a sustained recovery of at least 3-4 days.",
    "Cap maximum forecast values at the most recent historical low minus 1.5% for the first 5 days of a new forecast cycle if the previous cycle ended in a sharp decline.",
    "Ignore positive sentiment signals (e.g., +0.50) if they occur after a multi-day downtrend; the model overreacts to these by projecting premature rebounds, whereas prices typically remain suppressed or continue drifting lower."
  ]
